Checks and results:
1. API key. openrouter-client.ts:18-27 passes the key only to the SDK constructor. The package source has no console call and no fetch call. mapSdkError copies only the status and the message into a new Error, so the SDK body, headers, and raw response do not travel on. The SDK error classes build their text from the response body or the cause, never from request headers.
2. Env read. The key is read at call time inside the two resolve functions, on the server. No use-client file imports the package.
3. Routes. The S1 range changes neither chatbot route. In BM2, auth runs at route.ts:77-84, the rate limit at :89-106, and the provider at :181. In IM3, auth runs at :85-92, enrollment at :147-157, the rate limit at :159-177, and the provider at :209. Both 503 bodies are the fixed string AI provider not configured. Student-visible errors are fixed strings. The spreadsheet route swallows provider errors.
4. workerd probe. It uses the dummy key probe-key, a loopback mock, wrangler dev with --local, and a fixed argv. wrangler is a local dependency, so npx downloads nothing. The CI step has no env block and no secret. The Green log shows probe-ok. I did not run the probe.
5. Dependency. License Apache-2.0. The postinstall script is node scripts/check-types.js || true. It returns when CI is set and skips when src/types/models.ts is absent, so it makes no request in an installed copy. The lockfile adds one package. zod dedupes to 4.6.7. npm audit equals the baseline by package, severity, and advisory source (21 of 21). No advisory names @openrouter/sdk or zod. npm audit signatures reports no failure on the second run (the first run hit ECONNRESET on prettier).
6. SDK network use. The analytics hostnames in the SDK are Zod default values in management-API schemas. No code calls them. The request body adds only stream:false. No identifier is added.
7. Secrets. The added lines hold only the fake keys test-key, sk-test, sdk-route-key, and probe-key. No env file, key file, or credential file is in the range.
8. Tests at the audited HEAD. The package provider tests pass (23, with the 6 SDK transport cases). The BM2 SDK route and provider tests pass (3). The IM3 SDK route test passes (1). No test reaches the network.
9. A2 is not applicable. A6 is not applicable: measure/tracks.md is not in the range and holds no resolved security claim for this track.

